## Shenzhen and Dongguan buildings — Overture, 3D-GloBFP, CTBUH 深圳、东莞建筑

On the Greater Bay page, the Shenzhen and Dongguan buildings (`site/gbadata/gba_bld*.txt`, made by `src/gbareal/szdg/`) come from three sources:
大湾区页面上深圳、东莞的楼（`site/gbadata/gba_bld*.txt`，由 `src/gbareal/szdg/` 生成）来自三个来源：

- **Footprints 轮廓**: Overture Maps buildings, release 2026-11-18.0. In Shenzhen and Dongguan these are OpenStreetMap buildings (ODbL) and the *East Asian buildings* machine-learning footprints by Shi et al. (Zenodo doi:10.5281/zenodo.8174931, CC BY 4.0). Credit: “© OpenStreetMap contributors, Overture Maps Foundation” and Shi et al. https://docs.overturemaps.org/attribution/
  Overture Maps 2026-11-18.0 版的建筑：在深圳、东莞是 OpenStreetMap 的楼（ODbL）和 Shi 等人的“东亚建筑”机器学习轮廓（CC BY 4.0）。
- **Heights of ordinary buildings 普通楼的高度**: where OpenStreetMap has no height or floor count, the height is from 3D-GloBFP (Che et al. 2024, *Earth System Science Data* 16:5357; Zenodo 15487006; CC BY 4.0). These are machine-learning estimates for the year 2020, about ±13 m, and far too low for towers. Buildings with no 3D-GloBFP match get an estimate by footprint size.
  OpenStreetMap 没有高度或层数的楼，用 3D-GloBFP 的高度（机器学习估算，2020 年，误差约 ±13 米，高楼严重偏低）。连 3D-GloBFP 也没有的，按占地面积估算。
- **Heights of tall buildings 高楼的高度**: the CTBUH Skyscraper Center (https://www.skyscrapercenter.com/), cross-checked with Wikipedia (CC BY-SA), Wikidata (CC0) and OpenStreetMap; lists in `src/gbareal/szdg/data/`. CTBUH information is available for public use when CTBUH is cited. Unfinished towers (under construction, stalled, on hold) do not get their planned height.
  高楼高度来自 CTBUH（国际高层建筑与都市人居学会），并用维基百科、维基数据和 OpenStreetMap 核对；清单在 `src/gbareal/szdg/data/`。引用 CTBUH 即可公开使用。未建成的楼（在建、停工、搁置）不用规划高度。

Building types and facade colours are our approximations, not data.
建筑类型和外墙颜色是我们的近似，不是数据。

## Terrain 地形

Terrain heights come from AWS Terrain Tiles (Mapzen / Tilezen terrarium tiles, zoom 12):
https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/

The registry points at the Tilezen attribution list:
https://github.com/tilezen/joerd/blob/master/docs/attribution.md

These five cities do not use the whole global mix. The sources that apply here are:

- San Francisco Bay Area and New York: USGS 3DEP, plus SRTM and GMTED2010, courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey. Public domain in the United States. The USGS asks for credit when you publish or redistribute.
- Singapore, Hong Kong and Tokyo, and the coarser fill everywhere: SRTM and GMTED2010, courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey. SRTM is distributed by the USGS; a copyright notice is asserted for products distributed outside the United States, and no copyright is claimed under the US Copyright Act. Credit is requested.
- Sea floor and water fill: ETOPO1, U.S. National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA). Public domain in the United States. Not for navigation. A work made mostly of this material should say that the U.S. Government material in it is not copyrighted in the United States.

Suggested credit 建议署名：

> 3DEP, SRTM and GMTED2010 terrain data courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey. ETOPO1 terrain data courtesy of the U.S. National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration.

这五座城市没有用到全球图块里的其他国家高程（ArcticDEM、澳大利亚、奥地利、加拿大、EU-DEM、墨西哥、新西兰、挪威、英国环境署等）。如果以后把地图扩到那些地区，再按上面的 Tilezen 清单补署名。

The corner of the map also carries a short “Terrain · USGS / NOAA” line so the credit sits next to the map, not only in this file.
地图角落还有一行短的 “Terrain · USGS / NOAA”，让地形署名和地图放在一起，而不只写在这个文件里。
